<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Hris.Foundation.Caching
    Sprint 8 (Kernel-Dependent Frameworks, Round 2) scope, per IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md
    Phase 1. Source specification: docs/03-foundation/caching-framework.md.

    No MediatR package and no MediatR requests of its own, the same shape Logging
    Framework's own csproj header states for itself, for a related but distinct
    reason: caching-framework.md describes no user-driven business command lifecycle
    either, and unlike Logging (which issues one MediatR query against Configuration
    Framework for its own minimum-severity threshold), this Sprint's own build issues
    no query against any of its four stated Upstream Dependencies (Configuration,
    Event, Logging, Tenant); see DependencyInjection.cs's own remarks for why each
    is a real dependency with no concrete integration point yet, not a gap.

    No EF Core persistence either: caching-framework.md's own Scope section names
    "Permanent Data Storage" as explicitly excluded, so there is no
    IEntityTypeConfiguration<T> here and no ProjectReference to Hris.Infrastructure.
    Microsoft.Extensions.Caching.Memory is this Sprint's own one concrete cache
    provider (in-process, single-instance). Redis or another distributed provider is
    a future, interchangeable implementation of the same ICacheProvider contract, the
    identical "one concrete implementation now, interface allows a future swap"
    precedent Logging Framework's own Serilog-only sink already establishes.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Hris.Foundation.Caching</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Caching.Memory" Version="9.0.4" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="9.0.4" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Hris.SharedKernel\Hris.SharedKernel.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
